# Judge calls (GAME-18): players call a judge, a judge claims the call and rules. An open call
# pauses the table timer. An expired deadline opens a call by itself and never decides for the
# player; the judge does. Disqualification (tournaments) is not an oust: nobody gains VP or pool.
seed 13
tournament
seat A alice
seat B bob
seat C carol
seat D dave
crypt A "Vera Nightfall" *8
library A "Iron Ward" *20
crypt B "Tomas Grey" *8
library B "Signal Fire" *20
crypt C "Ilse Várga" *8
library C "Quick Feed" *20
crypt D "Tomas Grey" *8
library D "Signal Fire" *20
start
present A yes
present B yes
present C yes
present D yes
wait 10m
expect elapsed 10m

# Bob has a rules question. The call stops the clock until a judge has ruled.
B> call rules Does Iron Ward stack?
expect calls rules
log public B called a judge (rules question): “Does Iron Ward stack?”
reject:no-change B> call other
reject:forbidden B> claim
wait 10m
expect elapsed 10m
judge> claim
expect calls rules@judge
log public A judge is handling the judge call
reject:forbidden judge2> rule answered
judge> rule answered Yes, it does
expect calls none
log public A judge ruled: answered at the table: “Yes, it does”
wait 5m
expect elapsed 15m

# A slow-play call: the judge adds the time it took back to the timer.
C> call slow-play D
judge2> rule time 10
log public A judge ruled: 10 minutes added to the timer

# Alice, whose turn it is, goes away. When her deadline runs out a judge is called, and her turn
# isn't played for her. The judge gives her 12 more hours.
present A no
wait 24h
expect deadline A expired
expect calls deadline:A
expect waiting A:phase
judge> rule extend A 12
log public A judge ruled: A gets 12 more hours
expect deadline A reminded
expect calls none
# She runs out again, then comes back: the call settles itself and she plays on.
wait 12h
expect calls deadline:A
present A yes
expect calls none
log public The judge call is settled: the player decided

# Bob wants a say at phase ends, then goes away holding the impulse: the judge passes for him.
B> autopass none
A> next
expect window phase unlock
expect impulse B
present B no
wait 24h
expect calls deadline:B
judge> rule passfor B
expect calls none
expect window none
expect turn 1 A master
present B yes

# Dave abandoned the game: the judge disqualifies him. His predator gains nothing.
C> call other D
judge> rule disqualify D Left without telling a judge
expect disqualified D true
expect ousted D true
expect pool D 0
expect vp C 0
expect pool C 30
log public D was disqualified
